<title>SWEDEN: Ericsson signs $19 mln Poland contract.</title>
<headline>Ericsson signs $19 mln Poland contract.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish telecoms group AB LM Ericsson said on Tuesday it had signed a contract worth $19 million with Telekomunikacja Polska SA to supply a telecommunications network in the eastern part of Poland.</p>
<p>Ericsson said in a statement the contract, for a DRA 1900 radio access network, included base stations and subscriber access equipment.</p>
<p>It said the installation would be completed in March 1998.</p>
<p>-- Abigail Schmelz, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1003</p>
</text>
